2. Current official AIP/JMP requirements (accessed 2026-09-22)

- AIP Author Instructions:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/author-instructions/
  Initial submission is a single compiled manuscript PDF (and a separate PDF
  for supplementary material, if any). LaTeX is accepted. AIP encourages the
  JMP-specific Overleaf TeX template; the live wording does not establish that
  conversion to REVTeX is mandatory for initial submission. The abstract is to
  be one paragraph, without citations/displayed equations, and up to 250 words.
  Required order includes acknowledgments, author declarations, data
  availability, appendixes, and references. COI and CRediT statements are
  required for all submissions.
- JMP journal page: https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jmp
  This establishes the intended journal and scope. No verified JMP-specific
  page/word limit applicable to this regular article was found; no limit from
  another AIP journal was imported.
- AI policy:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/policies-and-ethics/ai-policy/
  AI cannot be an author; authors remain responsible. Material/substantive use
  affecting findings should be disclosed with tool and purpose. The existing
  acknowledgment is conservative and compatible, so it was retained verbatim.
- Authorship:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/policies-and-ethics/authors/
  Accurate contact information, identification of the post-publication contact,
  and agreed CRediT roles are required. These facts cannot be inferred.
- Conflict of interest:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/policies-and-ethics/conflict-of-interests/
  Every article requires a disclosure. Funding and relevant actual/apparent
  interests must be reported; absence cannot be assumed by an auditor.
- Research data policy:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/open-science/research-data-policy/
  A data availability statement is required. The manuscript relies on code and
  generated figure data, so “no new data” would be misleading without a reasoned
  author decision; public deposit is preferable where appropriate.
- Accessibility:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/policies-and-ethics/accessibility/
  Alt text is required for visual content; the April 2026 announcement confirms
  the requirement applies now. Captions are not substitutes for metadata alt
  text. Implementation should use the JMP template/submission workflow rather
  than an invented macro in the current generic class.
- Research integrity:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/policies-and-ethics/research-integrity-and-publication-ethics/
  Original images/data and their provenance must be retained and supplied if
  requested.

The exact title and author were also verified as the already disseminated
